            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0396" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6231/290: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janerio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-02T16:00:00-03:00">February 2, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 2—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. My 26, February 2, 3 p.m. Aranha is still insisting that it is more important
                    to control the exchange value of the compensation mark (my telegram No. 18,
                    January 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d389-f1"/>) than it is to attempt to
                    prevent subsidies. I am endeavoring to persuade him of the error of this.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
